REJECTED (2), each with the reason written at the code:
 A-L1  a re-entrancy guard on the producer. Not reachable: after_draw pops the
       return stack BEFORE it captures, the in-play filter admits the single
       call site 0x4969CD, and two captures would be strictly sequential in
       any case because each runs after its inner draw has returned. Measured
       deep=0. Stated in tagpu_surf.h rather than guarded.
 R1-5  slog unsynchronised across the two threads. House pattern at 55 call
       sites in the DLL, not one of which locks; it carries no state and
       nothing reads it back. One lock for all of them or none.

